  m_Name: Carta_CidadeJardim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: Cidade-Jardim
  _titleEn: Garden City
  _category: 0
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "Bairros espa\xE7osos, com casas, trabalho e campo lado a lado e um cintur\xE3o
    verde em volta que impede a mancha urbana de crescer sem limite."
  _summaryEn: Spacious neighborhoods with homes, work and countryside side by side,
    and a green belt around them that keeps the city from spreading without limit.
  _realWorld: "Ebenezer Howard prop\xF4s a cidade-jardim em 1898, e Letchworth, na
    Inglaterra, come\xE7ou a ser constru\xEDda em 1903. Bairros como o Jardim Am\xE9rica,
    em S\xE3o Paulo, seguiram a ideia."
  _realWorldEn: "Ebenezer Howard proposed the garden city in 1898, and work on Letchworth,
    England, began in 1903. Neighborhoods such as Jardim Am\xE9rica, in S\xE3o Paulo,
    followed the idea."
  _tradeOffs: "Baixa densidade p\xF5e menos gente por \xE1rea, encarece a infraestrutura
    e o transporte, e as casas de Letchworth acabaram caras demais para os oper\xE1rios."
  _tradeOffsEn: Low density fits fewer people per area and makes infrastructure and
    transit pricier, and Letchworth's houses ended up too expensive for factory workers.
  _sources:
  - Label: Garden city movement (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_city_movement
  - Label: Letchworth (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Letchworth
